Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patch `13-dwarf-multicannon` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`1be5dfb5f`).

**Problem.** The dwarf multicannon could not be set up.

**Change.** New module `content/other/dwarf-multicannon`:
- Set-up in four stages, loading, firing, pick-up and decay, with the OSRS varps client plugins read (`dropcannon` stage, `rockthrower` ammo, `ownedmcannon` coord, `mcannon_decayed`).
- A cannon left behind by a logout, or one that decays, goes back to the owner's bank.

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: timers `mcannon_fire` 431, `mcannon_decay` 432.

**Tests.** `DwarfMulticannonTest` (7, integration).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): buildCache pass, `spotlessCheck` pass, `assemble` pass, `test` pass, `integration` pass, boot pass (Server ready in 7.310347166s). `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** Varps and locs from the cache; varp meanings as RuneLite's Cannon plugin reads them (BSD).

**Release note.** The dwarf multicannon can be set up, loaded, fired and picked up.

